From f8d1d8c4e9a4dca260c5a6539dfccafdf298106e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: UZDoom NX2 <uzdoom-nx2@users.noreply.local>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:58:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 67/70] Port to Nintendo Switch 2 (kaiHEN, libounce, OunceVK)
 with an SD write firewall

- Build with libounce's Switch2.cmake toolchain and headers (Cortex-A78C),
  link OunceVK (libEGL.a: Vulkan + EGL for SDL2), Switch 2 portlibs first.
- SD card write firewall (nx2_fsguard.c) installed in userAppInit before any
  constructor: every create/write/truncate/delete/rename/mkdir/rmdir/chmod/
  utimes/link outside sdmc:/switch/uzdoom-nx2 fails with EACCES; other file
  system devices are unmounted; the program refuses to start without it.
- Write policy (nx2_pathpolicy.c, pure C, host-tested): canonical paths,
  '..', device prefix, ambiguous names and characters refused.
- Video: VI2 default window (no binder queue on Switch 2), VK_NN_vi_surface
  at 1920x1080, 60 fps at 60/120 Hz with VRR allowed.
- volk: trampolines through vkGet*ProcAddr for extension commands OunceVK
  does not export (debug utils, surface caps 2, acceleration structures).
- Remove Switch 1 / emulator workarounds: TPIDR_EL0 bridge, nvhost-as
  compatibility, binder and Mesa GL wraps.
- Never touch sdmc:/.mesa (RDoom cleared Mesa's cache there).
- Home sdmc:/switch/uzdoom-nx2, output uzdoom-nx2.nro, French messages and
  loading screen.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
